"""NORA intent labelling (v9).

Gives every row of a file an Intent-L2 and an Intent-L4. Every row is read and treated the same way, whatever
produced it. Intent-L1 and all original columns are left untouched; two columns are added.

Where things live
  intent_taxonomy.json   all domain knowledge: L2 / L4 tree (TM Forum eTOM + Open APIs), phrasing rules with tiers,
                         shared pattern parts, vocabulary rewrites, clause connectors, decisions, sources.
  command-line settings  every threshold, model size and target; defaults are in build_parser().
  this file              methods only. No category, word list or threshold is written in a function.

Training stages (train(), each logged as "=== n/8")
  1 load              taxonomy + input file, column detection and profile
  2 clean             normalise, vocabulary rewrite, record markers, near-duplicate groups, boilerplate test
  3 representations   domain embeddings (PPMI-SVD + SIF), word / char TF-IDF, rule evidence, first-clause TF-IDF
  4 labels            rule + L4-name (+ semantic) votes -> Dawid-Skene -> confident-learning cleaning,
                      fallback consolidation and small-L4 merge
  5 L2 models         grouped split; baseline + 5 candidates; selection on calibration rows; production refit
  6 L4 models         one logistic regression per L2; joint L2 + L4 decision weight chosen on calibration rows
  7 discovery         UMAP + HDBSCAN topics with stability and promotion gates for new L2 / L4
  8 outputs           final decision for every row, integrity checks, Excel, validation workbook, 3D maps, model

Train:  python intent_l2_l4_pipeline_v9.py --input data.csv
Score:  python intent_l2_l4_pipeline_v9.py --mode score --model <outdir>/model/intent_model.joblib --input new.csv
"""

